# Base config for the challenge-instance HTTP ingress (#319, ADR-0036 §4).
#
# caddy-docker-proxy merges this global-options block with the per-instance site
# blocks it generates from container labels (caddy=<sub>.<domain> +
# caddy.reverse_proxy). The provisioner sets those labels at container create;
# the ingress configures itself with no control-plane round-trip.
#
# `local_certs` makes Caddy issue every instance certificate from its own
# INTERNAL CA instead of a public ACME CA — the zero-DNS, zero-secret path for
# local dev + the e2e harness (paired with sslip.io wildcard DNS).
#
# PRODUCTION: delete `local_certs` and issue real certs via ACME DNS-01 — the
# global option is `acme_dns <provider> …` (NOT a `tls {…}` block, which is
# site-level and invalid here). Each instance subdomain is then issued a cert via
# a DNS challenge, e.g.:
#
#   {
#       acme_dns cloudflare {env.CF_API_TOKEN}
#   }
#
# See docs/CHALLENGE_INSTANCES.md for the wildcard-DNS + provider setup.
{
	local_certs
}
